Subject: [PATCH 4/8] refactor(zsh): enable autoloading and remove inline
 functions

Configure fpath to autoload custom functions from ~/.config/zsh/functions/
and remove all 171 inline function definitions from .zshrc.

Changes:
- Add fpath configuration with typeset -U for uniqueness
- Enable autoload -Uz for all functions in functions directory
- Remove 2,443 lines of function definitions
- .zshrc reduced from 2,690 to 247 lines (91% reduction)

Functions are now lazy-loaded on first use, improving shell startup
performance. All functions tested and working correctly via autoload.
